IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lb74-nouns`

-- Row il-74. THE REFERENCE, as typed values: one item, I1 (item 1, paragraph (e), of the Third Schedule of the Law), the section of the National Insurance Law it cites, the periods the instruments read print for that section, and the days the row computed from them.
-- Tests of the controls are in lb74-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in lb74-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (four: R1 and R2, each under each counting convention) are in lb74-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNNN-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew read from the deposited page image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNNN, printed page PPPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/). They are official instruments. Footnote numbers and quotation marks the pages print around an inserted text are left out of the quoted lines.
-- `tr:[tag] | LATIN` lines give the Latin form of words quoted on the lines above them, and tools/translit.py checks them against the Hebrew and against the string literals below.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.
-- A date typed as `the issue date its footer prints` is the date of the issue, and it is never a day of effect. A day typed in a `A day the row computed` is a COMPUTATION from printed values; no page prints it.

§ `References`

