-- ===== THE DAYS THE ROW COMPUTED (no page prints any of them) =====
-- 29.9.2009 plus 30 calendar months is 29.3.2012. If the start day is day 1 of the 30 months, the last day of the period is 28.3.2012; if the months are counted from the day after the start day, it is 29.3.2012. The row types both and chooses neither.
`the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months, as the row computed it` MEANS
    `A day the row computed` WITH
        `the day` IS Date 28 3 2012
        `the computation` IS "29.9.2009 plus 30 calendar months is 29.3.2012; with the start day as day 1 of the months, the last day is the day before: 28.3.2012"
        `what it is computed from` IS "the start day (29 September 2009) and the number of months (30), both printed in SH 2232 section 1"

`the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day, as the row computed it` MEANS
    `A day the row computed` WITH
        `the day` IS Date 29 3 2012
        `the computation` IS "29.9.2009 plus 30 calendar months is 29.3.2012; counted from the day after the start day, the last day is that day: 29.3.2012"
        `what it is computed from` IS "the start day (29 September 2009) and the number of months (30), both printed in SH 2232 section 1"

